    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d87">

                <pb facs="0193" n="947" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v02/pg947"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 600.119/410</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Commercial Adviser of the British Embassy</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Crawford</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Counselor
                        for the Department of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Polk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-09-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 22, 1917</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received September 24.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Polk</hi>: I enclose copy of a letter which
                    Percy has written to Mr. McCormick. I think that if you agree with the course
                    proposed this procedure will be the most practical, and we will send you on each
                    occasion a copy of the lists thus submitted to the board.</p>
                <p>Yours very sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">R. Crawford</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>




